import{_ as s,o as i,c as a,a7 as t}from"./chunks/framework.DUCm5Bu5.js";const k=JSON.parse('{"title":"Quickstart","description":"Start an isolated local server from a built checkout and check that it is alive.","frontmatter":{"title":"Quickstart","description":"Start an isolated local server from a built checkout and check that it is alive.","updated":"2026-10-18T00:00:00.000Z"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/getting-started/quickstart.md","filePath":"en/getting-started/quickstart.md"}'),n={name:"en/getting-started/quickstart.md"};function o(h,e,l,r,d,p){return i(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[t('<p>This page takes a checkout that you built in <a href="./installation">Installation</a> and starts a local, isolated server with in-memory persistence. It uses the game-less <code>management</code> profile for the first success check, then explains how a game profile such as <code>kr-812</code> differs, and what the checks prove and do not prove.</p><p><strong>Who this is for:</strong> someone who has finished the source build and wants a running local server within a few minutes.</p><h2 id="what-this-gets-you" tabindex="-1">What this gets you <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-this-gets-you" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What this gets you&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A local server process you can start and stop safely, with in-memory persistence and no connection to a real database. Accounts and progress reset when the process exits. It is not a playable complete server, and it is not evidence that a game client works.</p><p>The <code>management</code> profile starts the administration API and WebUI with no game or relay listener, so it works without client data. A game profile such as <code>kr-812</code> additionally requires local client data for that build, which the repository does not contain.</p><h2 id="before-you-start" tabindex="-1">Before you start <a class="header-anchor" href="#before-you-start" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Before you start&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><a href="./installation">Installation</a> is complete: the solution built with zero warnings and the build output exists.</li><li>A terminal is open at the repository root; every command on this page runs there.</li><li>The .NET 10 SDK is available: <code>dotnet --version</code> reports a 10.x version.</li><li>The local-check patch exists. Check it in PowerShell with <code>Test-Path tools/local-checks/isolated-memory.patch.yaml</code>, or in a POSIX shell with <code>test -f tools/local-checks/isolated-memory.patch.yaml</code>.</li><li>You create the <code>.env</code> file in the next step.</li><li>Optional: if you want to start <code>kr-812</code> in this session, the matching client data exists under <code>client-data/kr-812/data</code> or <code>client-data/kr-812/dataraw</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="prepare-the-local-environment-file" tabindex="-1">Prepare the local environment file <a class="header-anchor" href="#prepare-the-local-environment-file" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Prepare the local environment file&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The profiles interpolate environment variables while they are composed, before any patch disables a service. That is why the local MySQL password variable must be present even for an in-memory check.</p><h3 id="_1-copy-the-example-file" tabindex="-1">1. Copy the example file <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-copy-the-example-file" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1. Copy the example file&quot;">​</a></h3><p>PowerShell:</p><div class="language-powershell vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">powershell</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">Copy-Item</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> .env.example .env</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Linux shell:</p><div class="language-sh vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">sh</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">cp</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> .env.example</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> .env</span></span></code></pre></div><p><code>.env</code> is git-ignored. Never commit it.</p><h3 id="_2-set-a-disposable-password" tabindex="-1">2. Set a disposable password <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-set-a-disposable-password" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2. Set a disposable password&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Open <code>.env</code> and set <code>BFF_MYSQL_PASSWORD</code> to a nonempty disposable value, for example <code>isolated-check-only</code>. The <code>persistence.mysql</code> row reads <code>${BFF_MYSQL_PASSWORD}</code> with no default, so composition fails when the variable is missing; the isolated-memory patch disables that row only after composition. Keep real database credentials out of local checks and use them only in a deliberately configured deployment.</p><p><strong>Check it worked:</strong> <code>.env</code> exists (<code>Test-Path .env</code> prints <code>True</code>) and its <code>BFF_MYSQL_PASSWORD</code> line is nonempty. Do not paste the file or its values into a chat or an issue.</p><h2 id="find-a-profile" tabindex="-1">Find a profile <a class="header-anchor" href="#find-a-profile" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Find a profile&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A profile names a client build and composes the plugin rows that build uses. Its id is <code>&lt;region&gt;-&lt;wire version&gt;</code>, and the number is the client&#39;s <code>ClientVersion_Major</code>, not the executable&#39;s file version. <code>management</code> is the administration-only profile; <code>setup</code> is the first-run assistant.</p><h3 id="_1-list-the-packaged-profiles" tabindex="-1">1. List the packaged profiles <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-list-the-packaged-profiles" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1. List the packaged profiles&quot;">​</a></h3><div class="language-powershell vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">powershell</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">dotnet run </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">project src</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">/</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">BubbleFighter.Fantasy.Host </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">c Release </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> profiles list</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The command prints one line per profile: the id and a description. This release lists 19. Two useful lines are <code>management</code> (&quot;Administration and durable storage only; no game or relay ports.&quot;) and <code>kr-812</code> (&quot;Korean 2015 client build, ClientVersion_Major 812, resource patch 458.&quot;).</p><p>A listed profile does not mean every gameplay feature for that build is implemented; available features and required data differ between profiles.</p><h3 id="_2-list-the-discovered-plugins" tabindex="-1">2. List the discovered plugins <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-list-the-discovered-plugins" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2. List the discovered plugins&quot;">​</a></h3><div class="language-powershell vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">powershell</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">dotnet run </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">project src</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">/</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">BubbleFighter.Fantasy.Host </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">c Release </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> plugins list</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The command prints one line per plugin definition: the plugin id, its version, the client builds it supports and where it was loaded from. This is the set of implementations the host can mount into a profile.</p><p><strong>Check it worked:</strong> both commands exit successfully and print lines; no profile or plugin scan error appears.</p><h2 id="check-the-effective-configuration" tabindex="-1">Check the effective configuration <a class="header-anchor" href="#check-the-effective-configuration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Check the effective configuration&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Compose the <code>kr-812</code> profile with the local-check patch and print the result without starting anything:</p><div class="language-powershell vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">powershell</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">dotnet run </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">project src</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">/</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">BubbleFighter.Fantasy.Host </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">c Release </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> run </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">profile kr</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">812</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;"> --</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">patch tools</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">/</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">local</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">checks</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">/</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">isolated</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">memory.patch.yaml </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">dump</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">config</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The command prints the effective row list as YAML and exits with code 0. Search the output for these rows:</p><ul><li><code>id: persistence.mysql</code> followed by <code>disabled: true</code>;</li><li><code>id: persistence.memory</code> with no <code>disabled: true</code> line, so it is enabled;</li><li><code>id: clientdata</code> with its resolved <code>data_directory</code> and <code>raw_directory</code> for <code>kr-812</code>.</li></ul><p>The isolated patch is applied last, so it overrides a developer <code>.env</code> or <code>local.patch.yaml</code> that points MySQL at a real database. The dump stops before any plugin activates, so it proves composition and validation only, not that the profile will start.</p><div class="warning custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">WARNING</p><p>A dump can contain interpolated values, including credentials, when a patch enables MySQL. Treat it as sensitive.</p></div><h2 id="start-the-server" tabindex="-1">Start the server <a class="header-anchor" href="#start-the-server" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Start the server&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_1-start-the-game-less-local-server" tabindex="-1">1. Start the game-less local server <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-start-the-game-less-local-server" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1. Start the game-less local server&quot;">​</a></h3><p>From the repository root:</p><div class="language-powershell vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">powershell</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">dotnet run </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">project src</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">/</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">BubbleFighter.Fantasy.Host </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">c Release </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> run </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">profile management </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">patch tools</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">/</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">local</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">checks</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">/</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">isolated</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">memory.patch.yaml</span></span></code></pre></div><p>When a repository-root <code>.env</code> exists, the first line says <code>Loaded unset variables from &lt;path&gt;.</code>. The server then prints its administration listener, the WebUI address and the active row count:</p><div class="language-text vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">text</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span>Row &#39;admin.http&#39; admin API listening on 127.0.0.1:8080.</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span>WebUI: http://127.0.0.1:8080/</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span>Server started with &lt;count&gt; active row(s).</span></span></code></pre></div><p><code>&lt;count&gt;</code> is the number of active rows printed by the host; it is not a fixed number. <code>management</code> has no game or relay ports. Its admin API base address is <code>http://127.0.0.1:8080</code>, which comes from the <code>admin.http</code> row in <code>profiles/bundles/core.yaml</code> (<code>${BFF_ADMIN_HOST:-127.0.0.1}:${BFF_ADMIN_PORT:-8080}</code>). The process stays in the foreground until you stop it.</p><h3 id="_2-start-a-game-profile-instead-needs-client-data" tabindex="-1">2. Start a game profile instead (needs client data) <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-start-a-game-profile-instead-needs-client-data" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2. Start a game profile instead (needs client data)&quot;">​</a></h3><div class="language-powershell vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">powershell</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">dotnet run </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">project src</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">/</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">BubbleFighter.Fantasy.Host </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">c Release </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> run </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">--</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">profile kr</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">812</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;"> --</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">patch tools</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">/</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">local</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">checks</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">/</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">isolated</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">-</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">memory.patch.yaml</span></span></code></pre></div><p>A game profile needs the matching client data. Without it, the <code>clientdata</code> row fails and startup stops with a message like:</p><div class="language-text vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">text</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span>clientdata: neither data_directory &#39;&lt;working-directory&gt;/client-data/kr-812/data&#39; nor raw_directory &#39;&lt;working-directory&gt;/client-data/kr-812/dataraw&#39; exists. Provision the configured client-data directories before enabling this row.</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Supply the data, or import it through the setup assistant described in <a href="./installation">Installation</a>, then start the profile again. With the data in place, <code>kr-812</code> binds its game listener on <code>${BFF_BIND_HOST:-0.0.0.0}:${LEGACY_PORT}</code>, which is <code>0.0.0.0:7110</code> because <code>profiles/kr-812/profile.yaml</code> sets <code>LEGACY_PORT</code> to <code>${KR_812_GAME_PORT:-7110}</code>. Legacy builds have no relay listener. The admin API stays on <code>127.0.0.1:8080</code>.</p><p><strong>Check it worked:</strong> the process stays in the foreground, prints the three startup lines above, and does not exit with an activation error.</p><h2 id="check-it-is-alive" tabindex="-1">Check it is alive <a class="header-anchor" href="#check-it-is-alive" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Check it is alive&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_1-check-the-health-endpoint" tabindex="-1">1. Check the health endpoint <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-check-the-health-endpoint" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1. Check the health endpoint&quot;">​</a></h3><p>PowerShell:</p><div class="language-powershell vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">powershell</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">Invoke-RestMethod</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> http:</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">//</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">127.0</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">.</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">0.1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">:</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">8080</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">/</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">health</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Linux shell:</p><div class="language-sh vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">sh</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">curl</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> -s</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> http://127.0.0.1:8080/health</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The response contains <code>status</code> = <code>ok</code> and a UTC timestamp. <code>/health</code> stays open even when an admin token is configured.</p><h3 id="_2-check-the-runtime-instances" tabindex="-1">2. Check the runtime instances <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-check-the-runtime-instances" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2. Check the runtime instances&quot;">​</a></h3><p>PowerShell:</p><div class="language-powershell vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">powershell</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">Invoke-RestMethod</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> http:</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">//</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">127.0</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">.</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">0.1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">:</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">8080</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">/</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">api</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">/</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">plugins </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">|</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> Format-Table</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> rowId</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">,</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> state</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Linux shell:</p><div class="language-sh vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">sh</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">curl</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> -s</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/plugins</span></span></code></pre></div><p><code>/api/plugins</code> returns the running plugin rows. Each item has <code>rowId</code>, <code>plugin</code>, <code>source</code>, <code>state</code> and <code>error</code>. Look for rows with <code>state</code> = <code>Active</code> and an empty <code>error</code>; a <code>Failed</code> or <code>Pending</code> row carries its diagnostic in <code>error</code>.</p><p>If you set <code>BFF_ADMIN_TOKEN</code> in <code>.env</code>, every <code>/api</code> call needs a bearer token: add <code>-Headers @{ Authorization = &quot;Bearer &lt;token&gt;&quot; }</code> to <code>Invoke-RestMethod</code>, or <code>-H &quot;Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;&quot;</code> to <code>curl</code>. The WebUI files and <code>/health</code> stay open so a browser can load the sign-in page.</p><h3 id="_3-open-the-webui" tabindex="-1">3. Open the WebUI <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-open-the-webui" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3. Open the WebUI&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Open <code>http://127.0.0.1:8080/</code> in a browser. The management profile serves the administration interface.</p><p><strong>Check it worked:</strong> the health response reports <code>ok</code>, the instance list shows active rows, and the WebUI loads. These checks prove that the host and its administration API run; they do not prove that a game client can connect.</p><h2 id="stop-the-server" tabindex="-1">Stop the server <a class="header-anchor" href="#stop-the-server" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Stop the server&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Press Ctrl+C in the terminal that runs the server. The console prints <code>Shutdown complete.</code> and the process exits. In-memory accounts and progress are discarded with the process; stopping is always safe for local checks because nothing durable was touched.</p><p>To keep data across restarts, switch persistence to SQLite or MySQL as described in <a href="./../guides/configuration">Server configuration</a>. The isolated-memory patch is for local checks only.</p><h2 id="what-this-does-not-prove" tabindex="-1">What this does not prove <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-this-does-not-prove" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What this does not prove&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>No game client logged in, and no gameplay or packet compatibility was exercised.</li><li>The management profile has no game or relay listener, so there was no client traffic at all.</li><li>A passing configuration or automated check is not native-client acceptance; test the intended login and gameplay flows with a real client, separately.</li></ul><h2 id="if-something-goes-wrong" tabindex="-1">If something goes wrong <a class="header-anchor" href="#if-something-goes-wrong" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;If something goes wrong&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong><code>environment variable &#39;BFF_MYSQL_PASSWORD&#39; is not set and has no default</code>:</strong> the <code>.env</code> file is missing, was not found at the repository root, or does not set the variable. Copy <code>.env.example</code> and set a disposable value.</li><li><strong>The administration port is in use:</strong> startup fails on the listener row. Set <code>BFF_ADMIN_PORT</code> in <code>.env</code>, or stop the process that owns port 8080.</li><li><strong>The game port is in use:</strong> set <code>KR_812_GAME_PORT</code> in <code>.env</code>, or stop the process that owns port 7110.</li><li><strong><code>kr-812</code> fails on <code>clientdata</code>:</strong> see the client-data message above; the build&#39;s data must exist before the profile can start.</li><li><strong><code>Server startup did not converge</code>:</strong> the message lists each non-active row with its state and diagnostic. Read the first <code>Failed</code> or <code>Pending</code> row and fix its cause.</li></ul><p>More cases are covered in <a href="./../guides/troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a>.</p><h2 id="next" tabindex="-1">Next <a class="header-anchor" href="#next" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Next&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Continue with <a href="./../guides/configuration">Server configuration</a> for persistence, ports, profiles and environment variables, then <a href="./../guides/plugins">Plugins</a> to learn how the plugin rows work and how to mount your own. For the companion launcher that installs clients and connects them to servers, see <a href="./../guides/launcher">Launcher</a>.</p>',75)])])}const g=s(n,[["render",o]]);export{k as __pageData,g as default};
